==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
**5 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Use [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] to defend against the Angels, along with rushers such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] to slowly chip away at Angelic Sleipnir and Camelle. Otherwise, Nukers such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can handle the periodic waves of Aku Gories, alongside some [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cats]] for assurance. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be timed on an opening against Angelic Sleipnir/Camelle for very high damage, since he can make use of most of his knockbacks thanks to low enemy damage.

